in two inside the sleeping bag.

263
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:42,920
Nah, just kidding.

264
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:44,510
Kakyoin!

265
00:16:44,593 --> 00:16:46,384
Hey, you sure you're all right?

266
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:48,537
Ha, please take a closer look.

267
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:51,337
Surely you know Hierophant
isn't that careless.

268
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:55,538
He wouldn't just stay on the enemy's
back without a plan in the wings.

269
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:03,860
He's not chopped in half.

270
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:08,520
He's turned into a snake-like thing,
and he's slithering into my ear!

271
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:23,100
Oh, my arm is moving on its own!

272
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:26,820
No, it's coming in!

273
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:33,680
I told you before,

274
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:37,842
my stand was in your blind spot,
and your scythe couldn't cut him.

275
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,257
Now then, unless you'd like to
be destroyed from the inside out,

276
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:44,634
how about you do me a favor
and heal the cuts on my arm?

277
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:46,797
Anything is possible in a dream, right?

278
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:49,300
So healing a cut should be easy

279
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:03,520
All right, everyone.

280
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:04,780
Time to wake up

281
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,360
Come on, Polnareff. Up and at him.

282
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,913
There's a nice breakfast waiting for you

283
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,497
I feel like I had a
terrible dream last night.

284
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:20,410
You and me both.

285
00:18:20,493 --> 00:18:25,220
I can't remember it, but I have the
sneaking suspicion that it was terrifying.

286
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:28,730
Kakuin!

287
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,260
Are you okay? How are you feeling?

288
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:33,080
I'm fine. What?

289
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:34,260
Are you positive?

290
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:37,277
Because you were acting like
a deranged lunatic last night.

291
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,478
You even carved letters in your arm.

292
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,960
Wait, what?

293
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,460
Where did the wound go?

294
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:45,980
All right.

295
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:48,771
I think I'll change the baby's diaper now.

296
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:50,960
What in the world?

297
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:54,040
It's morning, sleepyhead.

298
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:57,357
He seems to be getting along
famously with the baby.

299
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,616
Maybe I just dreamed the whole thing.

300
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,480
Well then, did you have a good rest?

301
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:04,660
Oh, well, never mind.

302
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,040
Mm-hmm.

303
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,495
Everyone's forgotten.

304
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:17,238
A stand whose very existence
is completely forgotten.

305
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,620
What a strange creature.

306
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,760
But I haven't forgotten anything.

307
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:27,335
Since I brought my stand into the
dream with me, my memories are intact.

308
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:32,360
Listen, because you're just a
baby, I won't eliminate you.

309
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,140
I won't even injure you.

310
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:36,700
We'll take you to a nearby town.

311
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:39,314
You need to be returned to your mother.

312
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:42,560
However, don't come
anywhere near us again.

313
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:45,535
If you do, you'll have to be punished.

314
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,820
In a manner such as this.

315
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:53,140
Is that my poop?

316
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:04,420
Oh, Cochulein, I see you've made
some baby food for the little lad.

317
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,580
Yes, good work.

318
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:08,958
I'm sure he must be starving by now.

319
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:13,140
Hey, no, you wouldn't!

320
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:16,980
Eat up!

321
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,006
These yum-yums are delicious!

322
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:20,940
Say-yum!

323
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,080
This again?

324
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,518
What's the problem?

325
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,895
It's as if he doesn't like this stuff.

326
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,551
At this rate, I'll have to force-feed him.

327
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:33,570
Stop!

328
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,637
You can't force it, Mr. Joestar.

329
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:39,760
If you do, he'll just end
up hating it even more.

330
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,960
In special cases like this.

331
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:57,200
I told you it was delicious.

332
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:12,077
Joestar and the others have now
crossed the Arabian Peninsula

333
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:14,837
and are currently making
their way across the Red Sea?

334
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,540
as they prepare to enter Egypt. But!

335
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,520
Hey, old man.

336
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,081
Something's off.

337
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,461
You're going the wrong direction.

338
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:29,360
If you're headed to Egypt, shouldn't
you be traveling directly west? Hmm?

339
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,951
You seem to be heading toward that island.

340
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,457
That's right. Nice deduction.

341
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:38,305
I've had my reasons for
keeping this to myself.

342
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:42,337
But before we arrive in Egypt,
we need to make a slight detour.

343
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:44,773
Someone is waiting for us on the island.

344
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:45,950
Hmm.

345
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:49,518
He's a man who is extremely
important to our journey.

346
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:52,400
What is that supposed to mean?

347
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:14,937
All the old paintings on the tomb.

348
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:16,977
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

349
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:18,620
If you move too quick!

350
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:21,637
They're falling down like a domino.

351
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:24,317
All the birds are men by the Nile.

352
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,357
They've got the money on a bed.

353
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:27,957
Called crocodiles.

354
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:30,937
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

355
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:32,640
Fallen types with a hookah.

356
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:42,160
Walk like an Egyptian.

357
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:56,937
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

358
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:58,937
Spin around and they cross the floor.

359
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:00,520
They've got the moves.

360
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:03,597
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more.

361
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:06,237
All the school kids so sick of books.

362
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:08,297
They're like the punk and the metal band.

363
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,860
When the buzzer rings!

364
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:12,557
They're walking like an Egyptian.

365
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:15,197
All the kids in the marketplace say.

366
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,177
Walk

367
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:23,260
like

368
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,190
an Egyptian?

369
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,537
I ended up killing my friend.

370
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:31,980
There's nothing I could possibly do.

371
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:35,181
Allow me to thank you for
freeing me from the lab.

372
00:23:35,340 --> 00:23:37,457
I wouldn't believe it
if it wasn't right here.

373
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:39,057
Tell me your three wishes.

374
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:41,680
Do you have the ability to revive someone?
